-- Fixture for `l4 export dmn`'s empty-model refusal (smucclaw/l4-ide#1104),
-- with two reasons at once.
--
-- `sample amounts` is test scaffolding: it is referenced only as an argument
-- inside the #ASSERT, and --include-tests puts it back. `the payment` is a
-- regulative rule nothing calls, which the DMN export leaves out with or
-- without the flag. The refusal must name each under its own reason, and
-- offer --include-tests only for the first.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Payer, Payee

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF `pay the amount`

`sample amounts` MEANS LIST 100, 200

`the payment` MEANS
  PARTY Payer
  MUST `pay the amount`
  WITHIN 30

#ASSERT count `sample amounts` EQUALS 2
